// ◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉◉

// @function This function define the current trend and momentum force according to 4wma, 12wma, 21ema and 200sma
// @param FilterTrendWithMa50 is set to true will filter trend result with 50sma
// @param FilterTrendWithMa200 is set to true will filter trend result with 200sma
// @returns Return a positive value if trend is up (2 : strong momentum, 1 : weak momentum) and a negative value if trend is negative (-2 : strong momentum, -1 : weak momentum)
export calcTrendMom(bool FilterTrendWithMa50, bool FilterTrendWithMa200) => 
    vMa0 = ta.wma(close, 4)
    vMa1 = ta.wma(close, 12)
    vMa2 = ta.ema(close, 21)
    vMa3 = ta.sma(close, 50)
    vMa5 = ta.sma(close, 200)
    vMa0Var = vMa0 - vMa0[1]
    vMa1Var = vMa1 - vMa1[1]
    vMa2Var = vMa2 - vMa2[1]
    vMa3Var = vMa3 - vMa3[1]
    // strong mom up 
    conditionMomUpStrong1 = vMa0Var > 0 and vMa1Var > 0 and vMa2Var > 0     // mom 4+12+21
    conditionMomUpStrong2 = close > vMa2
    conditionMomUpStrong3 = FilterTrendWithMa50 == true ? close > vMa3 : true
    conditionMomUpStrong4 = FilterTrendWithMa200 == true ? close > vMa5 : true
    conditionMomUpStrong  = conditionMomUpStrong1 and conditionMomUpStrong2 and conditionMomUpStrong3 and conditionMomUpStrong4
    // strong mom up throwback
    conditionMomUpStart1 = not conditionMomUpStrong1 and vMa2Var > 0        // not strong and mom 21
    conditionMomUpStart2 = close > vMa2
    conditionMomUpStart3 = FilterTrendWithMa50 == true ? close > vMa3 : true
    conditionMomUpStart4 = FilterTrendWithMa200 == true ? close > vMa5 : true
    conditionMomUpStart  = conditionMomUpStart1 and conditionMomUpStart2 and conditionMomUpStart3 and conditionMomUpStart4
    // strong mom dn 
    conditionMomDnStrong1 = vMa0Var < 0 and vMa1Var < 0 and vMa2Var < 0     // mom 4+12+21
    conditionMomDnStrong2 = close < vMa2
    conditionMomDnStrong3 = FilterTrendWithMa50 == true ? close < vMa3 : true
    conditionMomDnStrong4 = FilterTrendWithMa200 == true ? close < vMa5 : true
    conditionMomDnStrong  = conditionMomDnStrong1 and conditionMomDnStrong2 and conditionMomDnStrong3 and conditionMomDnStrong4
    // strong mom dn pullback
    conditionMomDnStart1 = not conditionMomDnStrong1 and vMa2Var < 0        // not strong and mom 21
    conditionMomDnStart2 = close < vMa2
    conditionMomDnStart3 = FilterTrendWithMa50 == true ? close < vMa3 : true
    conditionMomDnStart4 = FilterTrendWithMa200 == true ? close < vMa5 : true
    conditionMomDnStart  = conditionMomDnStart1 and conditionMomDnStart2 and conditionMomDnStart3 and conditionMomDnStart4
    if conditionMomUpStrong
        result = 2
    else if conditionMomUpStart
        result = 1
    else if conditionMomDnStrong
        result = 2
    else if conditionMomDnStart
        result = 1
    else
        result = 0

// @function This function checks if close, 4wma and 12wma are in contraction within a multiple of the average true range
// @param AtrPeriod is the period used to calculate the average true range (ATR)
// @param AtrMultiplier is the multiplier of the average true range 
// @returns Return true or false
export calcPriceAmstNodeMa01(float close, int AtrPeriod, float AtrMultiplier) =>
    vMa0        = ta.wma(close, 4)
    vMa1        = ta.wma(close, 12)
    vMa0var     = vMa0 - vMa0[1]
    vMa0varvar  = vMa0var - vMa0var[1]
    t0          = math.max(vMa0, vMa1)
    t1          = math.max(t0, close)
    b0          = math.min(vMa0, vMa1)
    b1          = math.min(b0, close)
    cond1       = (t1 - b1) <= AtrMultiplier * ta.atr(AtrPeriod)
    cond2       = vMa0var > 0 and vMa0varvar > 0
    result      = cond1 and cond2  

// @function This function checks if close, 12wma, 21ema and 50sma are in contraction within a multiple of the average true range
// @param AtrPeriod is the period used to calculate the average true range (ATR)
// @param AtrMultiplier is the multiplier of the average true range 
// @returns Return true or false
export calcPriceAmstNodeMa123(float close, int AtrPeriod , float AtrMultiplier) =>
    vMa1    = ta.wma(close, 12)
    vMa2    = ta.ema(close, 21)
    vMa3    = ta.sma(close, 50)
    t1      = math.max(vMa1, vMa2)
    t2      = math.max(t1, vMa3) 
    t3      = math.max(t2, close)
    b1      = math.min(vMa1, vMa2)   
    b2      = math.min(b1, vMa3)
    b3      = math.min(b2, close)
    result  = (t3 - b3) <= AtrMultiplier * ta.atr(AtrPeriod)

// @function This function checks inside bar candle configuration
// @returns true or false
export calcPriceInsidebar() =>
    if high[1] > high and low[1] < low 
        result = true
    else
        result = false

// @function This function checks if close is over extended from the 12wma by a multiple of the average true range
// @param PeriodNorm is the lookback period to normalize distance between close and the moving average
// @param AtrMultiplier is the multiplier of the average true range 
// @returns Return true or false
export calcPrice12wmaExtended(float close, int PeriodNormalization, float ExtensionPercent) =>
    Ma          = ta.wma(close, 12)
    vMaRme      = close - Ma
    vMaRmeHigh  = ta.highest(vMaRme, PeriodNormalization)
    vMaRmeLow   = ta.lowest(vMaRme, PeriodNormalization)
    vMaRmeMid   = (vMaRmeHigh + vMaRmeLow) / 2
    vMaRmeN     = (vMaRme - vMaRmeMid) / (vMaRmeHigh - vMaRmeMid) * 100
    condRmel0   = vMaRme > 0 and close > Ma
    condRmel1   = vMaRmeN[1] > ExtensionPercent and vMaRmeN < ExtensionPercent
    result      = condRmel0 and condRmel1

// @function This function checks if close is over extended from the 21ema by a multiple of the average true range
// @param PeriodNorm is the lookback period to normalize distance between close and the moving average
// @param AtrMultiplier is the multiplier of the average true range 
// @returns Return true or false
export calcPrice21emaExtended(float close, int PeriodNormalization, float ExtensionPercent) =>
    Ma          = ta.ema(close, 21)
    vMaRme      = close - Ma
    vMaRmeHigh  = ta.highest(vMaRme, PeriodNormalization)
    vMaRmeLow   = ta.lowest(vMaRme, PeriodNormalization)
    vMaRmeMid   = (vMaRmeHigh + vMaRmeLow) / 2
    vMaRmeN     = (vMaRme - vMaRmeMid) / (vMaRmeHigh - vMaRmeMid) * 100
    condRmel0   = vMaRme > 0 and close > Ma
    condRmel1   = vMaRmeN[1] > ExtensionPercent and vMaRmeN < ExtensionPercent
    result      = condRmel0 and condRmel1

// @function This function checks if close is over extended from the 50sma by a multiple of the average true range
// @param PeriodNorm is the lookback period to normalize distance between close and the moving average
// @param AtrMultiplier is the multiplier of the average true range 
// @returns Return true or false
export calcPrice50smaExtended(float close, int PeriodNormalization, float ExtensionPercent) =>
    Ma          = ta.sma(close, 50)
    vMaRme      = close - Ma
    vMaRmeHigh  = ta.highest(vMaRme, PeriodNormalization)
    vMaRmeLow   = ta.lowest(vMaRme, PeriodNormalization)
    vMaRmeMid   = (vMaRmeHigh + vMaRmeLow) / 2
    vMaRmeN     = (vMaRme - vMaRmeMid) / (vMaRmeHigh - vMaRmeMid) * 100
    condRmel0   = vMaRme > 0 and close > Ma
    condRmel1   = vMaRmeN[1] > ExtensionPercent and vMaRmeN < ExtensionPercent
    result      = condRmel0 and condRmel1

// @function This function checks if close is over extended from the 200sma by a multiple of the average true range
// @param PeriodNorm is the lookback period to normalize distance between close and the moving average
// @param AtrMultiplier is the multiplier of the average true range 
// @returns Return true or false
export calcPrice200smaExtended(float close, int PeriodNormalization, float ExtensionPercent) =>
    Ma          = ta.sma(close, 200)
    vMaRme      = close - Ma
    vMaRmeHigh  = ta.highest(vMaRme, PeriodNormalization)
    vMaRmeLow   = ta.lowest(vMaRme, PeriodNormalization)
    vMaRmeMid   = (vMaRmeHigh + vMaRmeLow) / 2
    vMaRmeN     = (vMaRme - vMaRmeMid) / (vMaRmeHigh - vMaRmeMid) * 100
    condRmel0   = vMaRme > 0 and close > Ma
    condRmel1   = vMaRmeN[1] > ExtensionPercent and vMaRmeN < ExtensionPercent
    result      = condRmel0 and condRmel1

// @function This function checks if price is in climax evolution by comparing the extension between 4wma and 12wma, and a multiple of the average true range
// @param AtrPeriod is the average true range period
// @param MovingAvgAtrMulti is the extension ratio
// @param VolAtrMulti is the volume extension relative to the 21sma volume
// @returns Return true or false
export calcPriceClimax(float close, int AtrPeriod, float MovingAvgAtrMulti, float VolAtrMulti) =>
    vMa0                        = ta.wma(close, 4)
    vMa1                        = ta.wma(close, 12)
    vVolumeAvg                  = ta.sma(volume, 21)
    vVolHihestRatioLast2bars    = ta.highest(volume / vVolumeAvg, 2)
    vMaRelativeExtension        = (vMa0 - vMa1) / ta.atr(AtrPeriod) // absolute relative Ma0-Ma1 extension
    vMaRelativeExtensionVar     = vMaRelativeExtension - vMaRelativeExtension[1] // relative ma extension change (slope)
    condPriceClimaxVol          = vVolHihestRatioLast2bars >= VolAtrMulti
    condPriceClimaxMa           = vMaRelativeExtension > MovingAvgAtrMulti and vMaRelativeExtensionVar[1] > vMaRelativeExtensionVar
    result                      = condPriceClimaxMa and condPriceClimaxVol


